  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PrePhys 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'You are meeting with a research team to give feedback on their ideas
    for preclinical studies and finalize a plan before animal studies begin.


    <b>Physicians
    often help design preclinical lab and animal experiments to make sure they are
    relevant to human disease.</b>


    Is this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: Physicians use their knowledge of how the disease affects people,
    how treatments work, and what side effects matter most to patients to help guide
    lab and animal studies. Their input helps the research team choose the right
    models, endpoints, and measurements so the studies are relevant to human disease.
    In doing so, physicians increase the chances that the results will lead to treatments
    that are safe, effective, and truly beneficial for people in the future.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: PreClinical
